            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>\"A Christmas Carol\"</strong><br>\nOne of Dickens's most famous works, \"A Christmas Carol,\" was published in 1843. This novella, telling the story of Ebenezer Scrooge's transformation from a miser to a generous benefactor, remains a significant influence on the way Christmas is celebrated in the English-speaking world.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Writing Style</strong><br>\nDickens's writing style is marked by his use of caricature, wit, and pathos. His characters are some of the most memorable in English literature, with a vividness that has captured readers' imaginations for over a century.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life and Public Readings</strong><br>\nDickens had a tumultuous personal life, including a separation from his wife and a close relationship with the actress Ellen Ternan. In his later years, he gave public readings from his works, which were enormously popular and added to his fame.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
